Relevant tables / columns and their possible use  
• `associationByDatasourceDirect.targetId`: Ensembl gene ID to be linked with the gene catalogue.  
• `associationByDatasourceDirect.diseaseId`: lets us keep only the disease of interest (`'EFO_0000676'`).  
• `associationByDatasourceDirect.datasourceId`: allows restriction to the requested evidence source (`'IMPC'`).  
• `associationByDatasourceDirect.score`: overall (direct) association score – we need the gene(s) with the maximum value.  
• `targets.id`: primary key (Ensembl gene ID) to join with `targetId`.  
• `targets.approvedSymbol`: the human‑readable gene symbol we finally want to return.  

Typical conditions  
• `WHERE diseaseId = 'EFO_0000676'`  
• `AND LOWER(datasourceId) = 'impc'`  
• `ORDER BY score DESC` (to spot the highest)  
• `QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER(ORDER BY score DESC)=1` (to keep only top‑scoring rows)  

Exploratory → final SQLs  
```sql
-- 1) Peek at IMPC rows (any disease)
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.associationByDatasourceDirect`
WHERE LOWER(datasourceId) = 'impc'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Distinct diseases that have IMPC evidence
SELECT DISTINCT diseaseId
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.associationByDatasourceDirect`
WHERE LOWER(datasourceId) = 'impc'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) IMPC associations for the requested disease
SELECT targetId, score
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.associationByDatasourceDirect`
WHERE diseaseId = 'EFO_0000676'
  AND LOWER(datasourceId) = 'impc'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Same, ordered by descending score
SELECT targetId, score
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.associationByDatasourceDirect`
WHERE diseaseId = 'EFO_0000676'
  AND LOWER(datasourceId) = 'impc'
ORDER BY score DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Join to get gene symbols (top 20 by score)
SELECT a.targetId,
       t.approvedSymbol,
       a.score
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.associationByDatasourceDirect` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.targets`                 AS t
     ON a.targetId = t.id
WHERE a.diseaseId   = 'EFO_0000676'
  AND LOWER(a.datasourceId) = 'impc'
ORDER BY a.score DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Retrieve the maximum score for this disease / datasource
SELECT MAX(score) AS max_score
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.associationByDatasourceDirect`
WHERE diseaseId = 'EFO_0000676'
  AND LOWER(datasourceId) = 'impc';
```

```sql
-- 7) All genes that reach that maximum score
WITH m AS (
  SELECT MAX(score) AS max_score
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.associationByDatasourceDirect`
  WHERE diseaseId = 'EFO_0000676'
    AND LOWER(datasourceId) = 'impc'
)
SELECT a.targetId, a.score
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.associationByDatasourceDirect` AS a
CROSS JOIN m
WHERE a.diseaseId   = 'EFO_0000676'
  AND LOWER(a.datasourceId) = 'impc'
  AND a.score = m.max_score;
```

```sql
-- 8) Same as (7) but with the gene symbols
WITH m AS (
  SELECT MAX(score) AS max_score
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.associationByDatasourceDirect`
  WHERE diseaseId = 'EFO_0000676'
    AND LOWER(datasourceId) = 'impc'
)
SELECT t.approvedSymbol,
       a.targetId,
       a.score
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.associationByDatasourceDirect` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.targets`                 AS t
     ON a.targetId = t.id
CROSS JOIN m
WHERE a.diseaseId   = 'EFO_0000676'
  AND LOWER(a.datasourceId) = 'impc'
  AND a.score = m.max_score;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same goal using ROW_NUMBER instead of MAX
SELECT approvedSymbol, targetId, score
FROM (
  SELECT t.approvedSymbol,
         a.targetId,
         a.score,
         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY a.score DESC) AS rn
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.associationByDatasourceDirect` AS a
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.targets`                 AS t
       ON a.targetId = t.id
  WHERE a.diseaseId   = 'EFO_0000676'
    AND LOWER(a.datasourceId) = 'impc'
)
WHERE rn = 1;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final concise answer: approved symbols with highest IMPC overall score
SELECT DISTINCT t.approvedSymbol
FROM `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.associationByDatasourceDirect` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.open_targets_platform.targets`                 AS t
  ON a.targetId = t.id
WHERE a.diseaseId   = 'EFO_0000676'
  AND LOWER(a.datasourceId) = 'impc'
QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY a.score DESC) = 1;
```

